---
// DRAFT — have a solicitor review before launch.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { PRODUCT, SELLER, LEGAL_LAST_UPDATED, NOT_HMRC_NOTICE } from '../data/shop.js';
---
<Base
  title="Disclaimer — Making Tax Digital (MTD) Tracker and Checker | gazza.ltd"
  description="Important information about the Making Tax Digital (MTD) Income Tax checker and readiness tracker: not tax advice, not MTD software, and what they are based on."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs trail={[{ name: 'Disclaimer' }]} />

    <h1>Important information</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">Last updated {LEGAL_LAST_UPDATED}.</p>

    <p class="note note-warn not-hmrc" role="note"><strong>Not an official HMRC tool.</strong> {NOT_HMRC_NOTICE}</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        <strong>Not advice.</strong> The {PRODUCT.name} and the free MTD checker are
        record-keeping and planning aids. They aren't tax, legal, accounting or financial
        advice. They don't take your personal circumstances into account, and they don't
        work out how much tax you owe. If you're unsure about your position, speak to
        HMRC, an accountant or a tax adviser.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Not MTD software.</strong> The workbook can't send quarterly updates or
        tax returns to HMRC. Under Making Tax Digital for Income Tax these must be sent
        using HMRC-recognised software. A spreadsheet can only be used for MTD if you
        link it to HMRC-compatible bridging software, and this product doesn't include
        any. Use HMRC's software finder on GOV.UK to find compatible software.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>What it's based on.</strong> The content is based on GOV.UK guidance as at
        19 October 2026 and is set up for the 2027/28 tax year (6 April 2027 to 5 April
        2028). Rules, thresholds and deadlines can change. Always check the latest GOV.UK
        guidance before you rely on a date or figure. We don't promise to update the
        workbook for later changes or later tax years.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>What it doesn't cover.</strong> Exemptions and deferrals from MTD, foreign
        property income, partnerships, and more than one business of the same type. If
        any of these apply to you, the threshold check and summaries may not reflect your
        position.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Your records are your responsibility.</strong> You're responsible for the
        figures you enter, for checking what your software sends to HMRC, and for meeting
        HMRC deadlines. The totals in the workbook are only as accurate as the entries
        you make.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>If something's wrong.</strong> We've taken care to make the workbook
        accurate. If you spot an error, please tell us at
        {' '}<a href={`mailto:${SELLER.email}`}>{SELLER.email}</a> and we'll look into it.
        This doesn't affect your legal rights if the workbook is faulty. See our
        {' '}<a href="/refund-policy/">refund policy</a> and <a href="/terms-of-sale/">terms of sale</a>.
      </p>
      <p>Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
